      "worked": "Since $\\frac{y}{3}\\in\\mathbb Z$, $y$ is a multiple of 3. The largest allowed positive multiple is 12, since $12^2=144\\le150$ but $15^2=225>150$. Zero and the corresponding negative multiples also satisfy the conditions.\n$$\\{-12,-9,-6,-3,0,3,6,9,12\\}.$$",
